BorrowCapability
├── shared implementation
│   ├── deploys without constructor configuration
│   ├── serves multiple pools and assets through one installed selector
│   ├── identifies minimums by both health-call target and calldata
│   └── adapters have independent minimums retained across implementation replacement
├── borrow
│   ├── accepts and emits the flat target, health target, data and health data arguments
│   ├── requires a Merkle-authorized self-call and a positive configured minimum
│   ├── only the nested lending amount varies under the approved leaf
│   ├── changing any pinned protocol or health-call byte invalidates the proof
│   ├── passes Aave and Morpho calldata unchanged with dynamic amounts
│   ├── calls the protocol as the adapter without intermediate custody
│   ├── checks health after protocol callbacks and snapshots the minimum before the call
│   ├── reverts borrowing and transfers on protocol, query or health failures
│   └── also guards collateral withdrawals without blocking independent partial repayment
└── setHealthFactor
    ├── rejects direct calls including the adapter owner and owner callbacks
    ├── accepts only approved self-calls with a valid proof and leaf role
    ├── rejects missing roles, altered query IDs or masks, and stale roots
    ├── lets an authorized nonowner vary minimums without changing the root or roles
    └── requires a positive minimum but does not query or enforce current health
